  <section class="pp-image-text">
    <div class="pp-img-standard pp-img-large">
      <img src="/projects/dr-seuss-chess/content/models.jpg" alt="">
    </div>
    <div class="pp-text-image-right">
      <div style="height: 5vh"></div>
      <p class="pp-body">I wanted to learn poly modeling, so I started out in Maya. I got as far as making the silouettes, and then decided to switch to Solidworks--since it was just a two week project, I was running out of time, and I could make each piece in a matter of minutes.</p>      
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pp-text-image">
    <div class="pp-text-image-left">
      <div style="height: 5vh"></div>
      <p class="pp-body">Once I had all 32 pieces printed, I spraypainted half of them blue and the other half red. Then I hand painted them all with the main body color.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pp-img-standard">
      <img src="/projects/dr-seuss-chess/content/painting.jpg" alt="">
    </div>
  </section>

<section class="pp-image-text">
    <div class="pp-img-standard pp-img-large">
      <img src="/projects/dr-seuss-chess/content/maya.jpg" alt="">
    </div>
    <div class="pp-text-image-right">
      <div style="height: 5vh"></div>
      <p class="pp-body">I wanted to take this project to the next level and imagine what kind of world these buildings would live in.</p>      
      <p class="pp-body">&nbsp;</p>
      <p class="pp-body">I imported my models back into Maya, modeled a scene with rolling hills and a reflective sky, and rendered the world using Arnold Render.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

